Flayr Tune patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

XmlDocument parses with one recursive call per nesting level
(readNextElement -> readChildElements -> readNextElement), so text from a
project file could nest deep enough to overflow the host's stack. Flayr Tune's
pre-scan already bounds nesting by its tag cap, but the parser itself should
never trust the depth: give it a hard limit of 64 levels, beyond which the
parse fails (errorOccurred, so getDocumentElement returns nothing). Flayr
Chop ships the identical change. Applied by CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent
PATCH_COMMAND.

Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_core/xml/juce_XmlDocument.cpp FLAYR_PATCH juce-xml-depth-limit
Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_core/xml/juce_XmlDocument.h FLAYR_PATCH juce-xml-depth-limit

diff --git a/modules/juce_core/xml/juce_XmlDocument.cpp b/modules/juce_core/xml/juce_XmlDocument.cpp
index 55bc246..383db84 100644
--- a/modules/juce_core/xml/juce_XmlDocument.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_core/xml/juce_XmlDocument.cpp
@@ -403,6 +403,20 @@ void XmlDocument::readQuotedString (String& result)
 
 XmlElement* XmlDocument::readNextElement (const bool alsoParseSubElements)
 {
+    // FLAYR_PATCH juce-xml-depth-limit: the parser recurses once per nesting level, so
+    // untrusted text could nest deep enough to overflow the stack. Fail the parse instead.
+    constexpr int maxElementDepth = 64;
+
+    if (elementDepth >= maxElementDepth)
+    {
+        setLastError ("elements nested too deeply", false);
+        outOfData = true;
+        return nullptr;
+    }
+
+    ++elementDepth;
+    const ScopeGuard depthGuard { [this] { --elementDepth; } };
+
     XmlElement* node = nullptr;
     skipNextWhiteSpace();
 
